---
_label: "Navigation Guide"
---

This site uses a keyboard-first navigation system. All shortcuts work anywhere on the page except when you are typing in a text field.

## Site Search

Press `⌘K` (or `Ctrl+K`) to focus the site search in the sidebar. On mobile, this opens the navigation drawer and focuses the search input.

## Command Palette

Press `/` to open the command palette and search across all pages by title.

Type `>` at the start of the query to switch to commands mode, which lists available actions for the current page. Press `Tab` inside the palette to toggle between modes.

## Page Navigation

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `J` | Go to the next page |
| `K` | Go to the previous page |
| `U` | Go up to the section index |

Previous and next follow the order pages appear in the sidebar. Use `J` and `K` to move through sections without lifting your hands.

## Other Shortcuts

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Y` | Copy the current page URL to the clipboard |
| `⌘\` | Collapse or expand the sidebar |
| `?` | Show the full keyboard shortcuts reference |
| `Esc` | Close any open dialog or palette |

## Sidebar

The sidebar width is resizable - drag the right edge to adjust it. The width and collapsed state are saved in `localStorage` and persist across sessions.

On screens narrower than 900 px the sidebar is hidden and replaced by a slide-out drawer, opened by the menu button in the header.
